==Icelandic==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|biðja|lang=non}} (whence also the Danish {{term|bede|lang=da}}, Swedish {{term|bedja|lang=sv}} and Faroese {{term|biðja|lang=fo}}) from {{proto|Germanic|bidja-|lang=is}}. Cognate with Old Frisian [[bidda]], Old Saxon [[biddian]] (Dutch [[bidden]]), Old High German [[bitten]] (German [[bitten]]), Gothic {{term|𐌱𐌹𐌳𐌾𐌰𐌽|tr=bidjan|sc=Goth}}.

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|bað|báðum|beðið}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=is}} to [[ask]], to [[request]]{{jump|is|ask|s}}
# {{context|transitive|governs the accusative|lang=is}} to [[ask]] someone to do something, to [[request]] some action of someone{{jump|is|ask|s}}
#: ''Ég '''bað''' þig nú bara um [[greiði|greiða]].''
#:: I just '''asked''' you for a [[favour]].
# {{context|ditransitive|governs the accusative and genitive|lang=is}} to [[ask]] someone of something, to [[request]] something of someone{{jump|is|ask|s}}
# {{context|intransitive|lang=is}} to [[pray]]{{jump|is|pray|s}}
#: ''Ég '''bið''' til [[Guð]]s.''
#:: I '''pray''' to [[God]].

